    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "SUBSTANTIAL 4 BEDROOM DETACHED RESIDENCE ON MATURE C. 0.5 ACRE SITE - POSSIBLE DEVELOPMENT OPPORTUNITY\n\nA substantial four-bedroom residence on a mature c. 0.5-acre enclosed site in a highly sought-after in Naas town * May qualify for the Vacant Homes Grant *\n\nLissadell is an attractive two-storey family home extending to approximately 230 sq. m. (2,476 sq.ft.), set amidst a mature and private site of approximately 0.5 acre. The property is approached via a gravel driveway and is well screened by established trees, hedging and mature planting, creating a pleasant sense of privacy. This well-established garden features an impressive variety of trees and shrubs, including walnut, beech, ash, maple, birch, Scots pine, cherry, apple and sweet chestnut, complemented by colourful hibiscus, jasmine, flowering currant, roses and wisteria. Two garden ponds further enhance the natural setting, while the garden?s maturity and scale provide a rich habitat for birds and other wildlife.\n\nIdeally positioned on the Dublin Road, the property is easily accessible to the many amenities that Naas has to offer. The town centre is nearby, with a wide selection of schools, shops, restaurants, cafés, pubs and leisure facilities. The Odeon cinema is 5 minutes walk, and the neighbourhood commercial centre at Monread is 10 minutes walk. \n\nThe property is well served by public and private transport. A major bus route is located directly outside the property, while the M7 motorway is a two minute drive away, providing easy access to the wider road network. Sallins commuter railway station is also within easy reach, offering regular rail services to Dublin and other destinations.\n\nWhile the house would benefit from modernisation and renovation to create a more energy-efficient contemporary home, the generous accommodation, mature setting and excellent location provide considerable potential for the discerning purchaser.\n\nNaas and the surrounding area offer an outstanding range of sporting and recreational facilities, including gyms, tennis, GAA, soccer, rugby, hockey, basketball, athletics, swimming and equestrian activities. Golf enthusiasts are particularly well catered for with several excellent courses in the surrounding area, while racing is available at Naas Racecourse (five minutes walking distance from the property), Punchestown and the Curragh. Monread Park is walking distance, and Kerdiffstown Park is a seven minute drive.\n\nSituated just off the N7/M7 motorway, approximately 22 km south-west of the M50, Lissadell is ideally positioned for commuters and those seeking convenient access to Dublin, while also providing excellent connectivity to Kildare and the south and south-west of the country.\n\nLissadell represents a rare opportunity to acquire a substantial family home on a generous mature site in one of Naas?s established and sought-after locations, with significant potential for renovation and enhancement.\n\nThe property is zoned Existing/Infill Residential under the Naas Local Area Plan 2021 ? 2027, with local precedence for subdivision and intensification.\n\nOutside \nGravel driveway, glass house, paved patio, outside tap. The property is approached via a gravel driveway and is well screened by established trees, hedging and mature planting, creating a pleasant sense of privacy. This mature and well-established garden features an impressive variety of trees and shrubs, including a mature walnut and sweet chestnut, and several beech, ash, maple (white, Japanese, paperbark), birch, Scots pine, holly, yew, cedar, larch, elderberry, service berry, cherry, and apple; complemented by hibiscus, fuchsia, jasmine, flowering currant, pyracanthas; and climbing roses and wisteria. In spring, the ground bursts with snowdrops, bluebells, hyacinths, and daffodils. Two garden ponds further enhance the natural setting, while the garden?s maturity and scale provide a rich habitat for birds and other wildlife.\n\nServices \nMains drainage, mains water, oil-fired central heating and electricity.\n\nZONING\nThe property is zoned Existing/Infill Residential under the Naas Local Area Plan 2021 ? 2027 with local precedence for subdivision and intensification."
      },
